    "seconds": 44,
    "summary": "The fault was an enabled `cartFailure` flag. I set its default back to `off`, and the namespace is healthy again.\n\n**Root cause:** The `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `cartFailure` with `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"`. Every other flag defaults to `off`, so this one was the only fault-injection flag switched on. The cart service's failure path was active, which breaks cart and checkout flows. The cart and flagd deployments were rolled out at <time> with a restart annotation, which is when the bad state went live.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- Set `cartFailure.defaultVariant` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap. I changed nothing else in the file.\n- Ran `kubectl rollout restart deploy/flagd`. The flagd init container copies the flag file only at pod start, so it needed the restart to pick up the change.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The live ConfigMap shows `cartFailure` default `off`.\n- The new flagd pod (`flagd-8488c648d-5nl46`) is 2/2 Running, and its logs show it watching the flag file.\n- All 28 pods in `astronomy-shop` are Running with 0 restarts.\n\nI did not run an end-to-end checkout to confirm the storefront flow. I also could not read the flag file from inside the flagd pod, because that container has no `grep` or `cat`. Both checks rest on the ConfigMap and the restart logs.",
    "timed_out": false,
